+<!-- Generated by examples/tools/build.py from example.json and the verifier's output. Edit example.json. -->
+# 151 · A throttle kept across a config update turned into a copy loses the failures of the calls in flight
+
+[← All examples](../README.md)
+
+| Verdict | Categories | Severity if shipped | Change | Verified unit | Approach |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| **✗ Violation: counterexample found** | functional | medium | refactor, behaviour change not intended | [`RetryThrottling#reconfigured`](../../examples/apps/crosscut/src/main/java/net/terminalvalue/crosscut/retry/RetryThrottling.java) | [B9: Regression verification](../../lib/README.md) |
+
+> When a channel's service config is updated with the same retry limits, `reconfigured` hands back the channel's throttle itself, so the calls in flight, which hold it, keep counting their failures into the throttle the channel goes on using. The change hands back a copy with the same tokens and the same limits instead: every field agrees when it returns, and a failure recorded afterwards by a call in flight goes into the old object, which nothing reads, so a failing backend gets retries the throttle would have refused. The regression proof observes the identity relations within each version and refutes the change with `result == throttle`, which holds before and not after; the witness is a construction recipe, replayed in the interpreter and run on a JVM.
+
+Tags: [resilience](../README.md#tag-resilience), [aliasing](../README.md#tag-aliasing), [object-inputs](../README.md#tag-object-inputs), [own-checker](../README.md#tag-own-checker), [confined-change](../README.md#tag-confined-change)
+
+## The change
+
+Hand back a defensive copy of the throttle when the limits are unchanged, `new Throttle(throttle.limits)` with the tokens copied over, so that the caller cannot change the channel's throttle through the object it was given. The copy has the same limits and the same tokens, so it looked like the same throttle.
+
+**Before** ([`RetryThrottling.java`](../../examples/apps/crosscut/src/main/java/net/terminalvalue/crosscut/retry/RetryThrottling.java), line 31):
+
+```java
+ */
+public static Throttle reconfigured(Throttle throttle, ThrottleLimits limits) {
+    if (limits.maxTokens() == throttle.limits.maxTokens() && limits.tokenRatioMilli() == throttle.limits.tokenRatioMilli()) {
+        return throttle;
+    }
+    return new Throttle(limits);
+}
+```
+
+**After:**
+
+```java
+ */
+public static Throttle reconfigured(Throttle throttle, ThrottleLimits limits) {
+    if (limits.maxTokens() == throttle.limits.maxTokens() && limits.tokenRatioMilli() == throttle.limits.tokenRatioMilli()) {
+        Throttle kept = new Throttle(throttle.limits);
+        kept.milliTokens = throttle.milliTokens;
+        return kept;
+    }
+    return new Throttle(limits);
+}
+```
